"help.message" = "1. Click the arrow to expand or collapse the pocket.\n2. Right-click the arrow to enable Notch Blackout, which turns the entire top menu-bar row black while keeping menu-bar items clickable.\n3. Hold ⌘ while dragging an icon to move it across the divider.\n4. Open Menu Bar Manager to inspect items hidden by the notch or pushed off-screen.\n\nThe manager asks for Accessibility permission only if you choose to enable it. It reads menu-bar item names, descriptions, and positions. It attempts to open a menu or simulate a ⌘-drag only when you click the corresponding action.\n\nBarPocket does not request Screen Recording, Input Monitoring, or administrator privileges, and it does not use the network. macOS and individual apps may reject some item moves or AXPress actions.";
